# FuseBase MCP Server Environment Variables

# ==============================================================================
# 1. Direct Token Authentication (Recommended / Zero-Browser Mode)
# As defined in FuseBase guides:
# https://thefusebase.com/guides/table-database/connect-ai-agents-to-fusebase-dashboards-with-mcp/
# https://thefusebase.com/guides/fusebase-ai/connect-external-ai-agents-to-fusebase-with-mcp/
# Note: When tokens are configured, FUSEBASE_HOST & FUSEBASE_ORG_ID are auto-discovered via whoami.
# ==============================================================================
FUSEBASE_GATE_TOKEN=your_gate_mcp_token_here
FUSEBASE_DASHBOARDS_TOKEN=your_dashboards_mcp_token_here
# Or unified token:
# FUSEBASE_TOKEN=your_api_token_here

# ==============================================================================
# 2. Session Cookie Authentication (Interactive / Headless Playwright Mode)
# Required only if collaborating on Y.js CRDT WebSockets or using session cookies
# ==============================================================================
FUSEBASE_HOST=yourorg.nimbusweb.me
FUSEBASE_ORG_ID=your_org_id
# FUSEBASE_COOKIE=your_cookie_string_here

# ==============================================================================
# 3. Tool Tier Configuration
# "core" (default, 34 tools) or "all" (175 tools including databases, portals, CLI, automations, tokens)
# ==============================================================================
# FUSEBASE_TOOLS=all
